{"name":"Holly Fern","hex":"#8cb299","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"holly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various shrubs or (mostly) small trees, of the genus Ilex, either evergreen or deciduous, used as decoration especially at Christmas.","The wood from this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/holly"},{"term":"fern","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a group of some twenty thousand species of vascular plants classified in the division Pteridophyta that lack seeds and reproduce by shedding spores to initiate an alternation of generations.","A light green color inspired by the color of ferns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Holly fern","blocks":[{"text":"Holly fern or hollyfern is a common name for several different species and genera of ferns:"},{"items":["Cyrtomium falcatum in the genus Cyrtomium","Polystichum lonchitis in the genus Polystichum"]},{"items":["Arachniodes","Polystichum"]}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly_fern","wikidata":"Q5882347"},{"title":"Holly","blocks":[{"text":"Ilex or holly is a genus of over 570 species of flowering plants in the family Aquifoliaceae, and the only living genus in that family. Ilex has the most species of any woody dioecious angiosperm genus. The species are evergreen or deciduous trees, shrubs, and climbers from tropics to temperate zones worldwide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Ilex-aquifolium_%28Europaeische_Stechpalme-1%29.jpg/330px-Ilex-aquifolium_%28Europaeische_Stechpalme-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly","wikidata":"Q117085"},{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop 